WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.866 --> 00:00:09.200
Ah, this is such beautiful weather. It feels so nice out.

2
00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:12.333
The best thing to do on a day like this is run.

3
00:00:12.399 --> 00:00:15.666
- Let’s go, Pikachu!
- Ash, what are you doing?

4
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:17.033
Huh?

5
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:24.033
I found a Trainer!

6
00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:27.700
- Huh? Who are you?
- Can we help you with something?

7
00:00:27.766 --> 00:00:31.933
Number 99! And that’s going to be you!

8
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.533
Number 99? What are you talking about?

9
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.666
Pika?

10
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.433
Now, what do you think? I’m talking about you and I having a Pokémon battle.

11
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.233
- So you’re a Trainer, too?
- Yeah, that’s right.

12
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.233
Korrina’s my name. My partner’s over there.

13
00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:51.133
- Huh?
- Hey, is that...?

14
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:55.933
Ah!

15
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.800
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

16
00:00:58.866 --> 00:01:02.599
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

17
00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:05.399
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

18
00:01:05.466 --> 00:01:08.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

19
00:01:08.366 --> 00:01:11.500
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

20
00:01:11.566 --> 00:01:14.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

21
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

22
00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:20.433
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

23
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

24
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

25
00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:38.433
On the road to Shalour City and Ash’s next Gym battle,

26
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.833
our heroes have an unexpected encounter

27
00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:45.000
with a Trainer named Korrina, along with her partner, Lucario.

28
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.600
Lucario, the Aura Pokémon and the evolved form of Riolu.

29
00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:53.466
Lucario reads the thoughts of others

30
00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:56.233
and anticipates their movements by sensing their auras.

31
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.000
- Looks like a tough opponent.
- Pika!

32
00:01:59.066 --> 00:02:00.300
Wow, so cool!

33
00:02:00.366 --> 00:02:04.699
Ha! This is perfect. We’re in top form today.

34
00:02:04.766 --> 00:02:08.566
Yeah! So we’re on? We’re having a battle, right, here and now?

35
00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:13.400
Right. I wanted to do some training before I challenge the Shalour Gym anyway.

36
00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.866
Pika, Pika!

37
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.833
What do you know? The Shalour Gym. Are you Trainers too?

38
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.766
Huh?

39
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:21.566
Are you going to challenge the Shalour Gym?

40
00:02:21.633 --> 00:02:24.766
Uh-uh. We’re not challenging any Gyms on this trip.

41
00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:27.766
But as far as being Trainers, you guessed right.

42
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:29.333
Hi. I’m Serena.

43
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.066
Hi there. I’m Bonnie. This is Dedenne and this is my brother.

44
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.600
My name’s Clemont. It's nice to meet you.

45
00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:36.700
Na-na-na-na!

46
00:02:36.766 --> 00:02:39.299
My name’s Ash. Great to meet you.

47
00:02:39.366 --> 00:02:42.933
- This is my partner, Pikachu.
- Pika. Pikachu.

48
00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.533
Pikachu!

49
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.100
Okay, Ash, let’s go. Make the first move.

50
00:02:55.166 --> 00:02:57.833
You got it. Let’s do this, buddy.

51
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.200
- Quick Attack.
- Pika!

52
00:02:59.266 --> 00:03:01.366
Lucario, stop them.

53
00:03:05.566 --> 00:03:08.766
- Iron Tail, let’s go.
- Pika!

54
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:11.700
- Quick, block it.
- Pika!

55
00:03:11.766 --> 00:03:13.633
-Oh!

56
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.200
It deflected it.

57
00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:18.533
I’m getting the feeling that Lucario is capable of much more.

58
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.000
Beating it won’t be easy.

59
00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.500
Come on, Ash and Pikachu! You can do it.

60
00:03:22.566 --> 00:03:25.399
Let’s keep up the pressure, Pikachu. We’ll be fine.

61
00:03:25.466 --> 00:03:28.933
- Pika! Pika! Pika!
- Now, use Iron Tail.

62
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.466
- Dodge it, Lucario.
- Chu! Chu!

63
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:35.399
Now use Swords Dance.

64
00:03:43.166 --> 00:03:45.033
It raised its attack power.

65
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.766
Okay, Lucario. Bone Rush!

66
00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:55.233
-Pika!

67
00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:58.033
- No way.
- Pikachu. Oh, no!

68
00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.266
Na-na-na-na!

69
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:02.766
Hey, Clemont? Bone Rush is a Ground-type move, isn’t it?

70
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:06.500
Mm-hm. It’s super effective against an Electric type like Pikachu.

71
00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:10.233
Not only that, its attack power got a boost from the Swords Dance.

72
00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:11.600
Pikachu’s in big trouble.

73
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:14.399
All right. Now, that’s what I call a hit!

74
00:04:14.466 --> 00:04:17.599
Okay, let’s keep up the pressure with another Bone Rush.

75
00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:20.933
-Pikachu, get up now!

76
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.366
-Pika!

77
00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:28.099
- Oh!
- Attack one more time!

78
00:04:29.099 --> 00:04:30.233
-Pika!

79
00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.933
Pikachu, no!

80
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.800
Pika!

81
00:04:36.866 --> 00:04:38.466
-Pika!

82
00:04:38.533 --> 00:04:39.666
- Ah!
- Huh!

83
00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:43.566
Awesome. There it is. The Power-Up Punch.

84
00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:47.033
Pika...

85
00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:50.033
Pikachu! Are you okay?

86
00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:52.633
Well, all right, Ash, it looks like we won.

87
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.066
- Here’s a Sitrus Berry. This will help.
- Oh.

88
00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.633
Thanks a lot. This’ll make you feel better, Pikachu.

89
00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.333
That Pikachu of yours is pretty strong.

90
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.066
But you’re not going to be able to beat the Shalour Gym.

91
00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.800
- How can you be so sure?
- You see...

92
00:05:07.866 --> 00:05:11.300
I know the Shalour Gym Leader, 'cause it’s me.

93
00:05:11.366 --> 00:05:13.300
- What? No way.
- Huh?

94
00:05:13.366 --> 00:05:15.666
You’re the Shalour City Gym Leader?

95
00:05:15.733 --> 00:05:17.766
Wow. No wonder you’re so strong.

96
00:05:18.766 --> 00:05:21.900
Now, that’s 99 wins. One more to go.

97
00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:28.133
Uh! Nothing’s more embarrassing than a growling tummy,

98
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.333
but we really can’t help it at all,

99
00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.099
since Pokémon battles take a whole lot of energy.

100
00:05:34.366 --> 00:05:37.599
I know what you mean. I’m feeling kind of hungry, too.

101
00:05:37.666 --> 00:05:38.666
Pikachu.

102
00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:41.800
All right, so why don’t we all have a little lunch?

103
00:05:41.866 --> 00:05:43.800
- Yes, please!
- Huh?

104
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.333
I can’t believe Clemont made all of this.

105
00:05:54.333 --> 00:05:56.800
Delicious! Your cooking is number one.

106
00:05:56.866 --> 00:05:59.400
I appreciate the compliment. Thank you.

107
00:05:59.466 --> 00:06:04.200
How are the Poké Puffs? I used Pecha Berries to make the topping.

108
00:06:05.966 --> 00:06:10.400
- It looks like Lucario loves them.
- Really? I’m so glad.

109
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.400
Hey, Korrina. What’s that thing?

110
00:06:15.466 --> 00:06:17.466
Heh! Oh, this’s a Key Stone.

111
00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:19.833
- A Key Stone?
- I thought so.

112
00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.566
- It looks just like the one Diantha has.
- Diantha?

113
00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:25.799
- Wow, you met the Champion?
- Mm-hm.

114
00:06:25.866 --> 00:06:28.000
Yeah, we met her just the other day.

115
00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.799
We saw Diantha using her Key Stone

116
00:06:33.866 --> 00:06:36.200
with Gardevoir for its Mega Evolution.

117
00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.700
Korrina? Can your Lucario Mega Evolve too?

118
00:06:40.766 --> 00:06:45.433
Nope. You see, Lucario doesn’t have a Mega Stone yet.

119
00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.833
Oh, no Mega Stone?

120
00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.599
So you just have the Key Stone right now?

121
00:06:49.666 --> 00:06:51.833
Yup. My grandfather gave it to me.

122
00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.400
Oh, yeah, the first person ever to Mega Evolve a Lucario

123
00:06:55.466 --> 00:06:57.766
was one of my ancestors, isn’t that wild?

124
00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:00.200
- One of your ancestors?
- Yup.

125
00:07:00.266 --> 00:07:03.166
It’s part of the tradition at the Shalour City Gym

126
00:07:03.233 --> 00:07:07.266
to have a Gym Leader there with a Pokémon that can Mega Evolve.

127
00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:14.400
Now. Listen well. In order for Lucario to Mega Evolve,

128
00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:19.033
you’ll need a Key Stone as well as a Mega Stone.

129
00:07:19.099 --> 00:07:25.033
So I just need to go to Geosenge Town and get a Mega Stone.

130
00:07:25.099 --> 00:07:29.766
Mega Evolution is an Evolution that transcends all other Evolution.

131
00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:33.700
It goes without saying that you need both a Mega Stone and a Key Stone,

132
00:07:33.766 --> 00:07:38.466
but what is more important is the bond of trust between you and your Pokémon.

133
00:07:38.533 --> 00:07:43.233
Yup, yup, yup. We need a strong bond. I get it! I get it!

134
00:07:43.299 --> 00:07:47.133
Lucario and I will get strong together.

135
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.500
Okay, Grandpa, we’re going.

136
00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:56.433
We decided we needed 100 victories in a row before we went to Geosenge Town.

137
00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.799
That’s what Lucario and I have been doing.

138
00:07:59.866 --> 00:08:03.866
So when you challenged me, you were going for victory number 99.

139
00:08:03.933 --> 00:08:05.366
-Pika.

140
00:08:05.433 --> 00:08:10.133
But having 99 victories in a row? I know you’re a Gym Leader and everything,

141
00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.500
but that sounds a little hard to believe.

142
00:08:12.566 --> 00:08:16.066
Oh, I’ve got proof. See this?

143
00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.966
They’re footprints.

144
00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:21.799
Wow. They’re from Pokémon you battled against?

145
00:08:21.866 --> 00:08:24.700
Yup. I asked them to stamp their paws.

146
00:08:24.766 --> 00:08:27.900
Here’s a print from a Pangoro whose Trainer's name is Kramer.

147
00:08:27.966 --> 00:08:32.966
And this one is from a Krookodile with a Trainer named Seth and...

148
00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:37.400
- What’s the matter?
- I forgot to ask Pikachu to stamp its paw.

149
00:08:37.466 --> 00:08:38.933
-Pika.

150
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.933
Now, don’t mind me. There.

151
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.933
-That’s ketchup.

152
00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.733
Mm-hm. Mm-hm. Mm-hm. This is perfect.

153
00:08:49.933 --> 00:08:52.699
So that Lucario could Mega Evolve,

154
00:08:52.766 --> 00:08:55.366
not to mention beating the thunderbolts out of Pikachu.

155
00:08:55.433 --> 00:08:57.800
Now, that’s an offer we can’t refuse.

156
00:08:57.866 --> 00:09:02.333
We may not have been able to catch Gardevoir, but Lucario’s a done deal.

157
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.000
We’ll cop the Key Stone and Pikachu, ooh.

158
00:09:05.066 --> 00:09:07.600
We’ll get that Mega Stone from Geosenge Town

159
00:09:07.666 --> 00:09:11.666
and then both Lucario and Pikachu will Mega Evolve right on the spot.

160
00:09:11.733 --> 00:09:15.033
And when the Boss gets a load of the mound of Mega-Evolved Pokémon

161
00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.300
we put together, he’ll flip his lid.

162
00:09:17.366 --> 00:09:19.433
Then let’s set the stealing stage.

163
00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.666
Wobbuffet!

164
00:09:22.866 --> 00:09:27.133
One more Trainer left. Who’ll be my 100th straight victory?

165
00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:30.333
Maybe Serena? Or maybe Clemont?

166
00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.933
- Attention, Miss. Yes, you.
- Huh?

167
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.333
- Huh?
- Is that Lucario your partner?

168
00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.166
- Uh...
- Who’s that?

169
00:09:41.966 --> 00:09:44.233
Certainly nobody suspicious.

170
00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.900
We’re the Mega Evolution Consulting Group.

171
00:09:46.966 --> 00:09:48.600
Mega Evolution what?

172
00:09:48.666 --> 00:09:50.666
Our job is to give you a consultation

173
00:09:50.733 --> 00:09:53.199
concerning how strong your Pokémon will become

174
00:09:53.266 --> 00:09:56.566
and what kind of moves it’ll use once it Mega Evolves.

175
00:09:56.633 --> 00:09:59.766
We’re also aware that your Lucario wishes to Mega Evolve

176
00:09:59.833 --> 00:10:02.866
using the Mega Stone from Geosenge Town.

177
00:10:02.933 --> 00:10:04.266
Now, how do you know that?

178
00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.633
See, when it comes to Mega Evolution,

179
00:10:06.699 --> 00:10:10.199
we know everything there is to know, from soup to dessert.

180
00:10:10.266 --> 00:10:13.300
- Wow. That’s cool.
- Na-na-na!

181
00:10:13.366 --> 00:10:15.666
A thorough consultation is in order.

182
00:10:15.733 --> 00:10:18.633
- I sense our encounter was meant to be.
- Mm-hm.

183
00:10:18.699 --> 00:10:20.633
Wait. There’s no need.

184
00:10:20.699 --> 00:10:24.966
We’re already super strong anyway and as soon as Lucario Mega Evolves,

185
00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:27.833
we’ll become stronger than we ever were before.

186
00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:31.566
It’s a free consultation, so there’s no reason to decline.

187
00:10:31.633 --> 00:10:35.133
- Now, step right this way.

188
00:10:35.199 --> 00:10:38.566
We’ll need to take this as well.

189
00:10:38.633 --> 00:10:41.766
- That’s mine.
- Fear not. It’s safe with us.

190
00:10:41.833 --> 00:10:44.000
Hey!

191
00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.500
Since we’re here anyway, we’ll look into Pikachu’s Mega Evolution.

192
00:10:48.566 --> 00:10:49.800
- Huh?
- Pika

193
00:10:49.866 --> 00:10:53.366
We’ll tell you everything, like how strong Pikachu will become

194
00:10:53.433 --> 00:10:56.300
when you use the Mega Stone from Geosenge Town.

195
00:10:56.366 --> 00:10:57.300
Now...

196
00:10:57.366 --> 00:10:59.000
Pik! Pika! PIka!

197
00:10:59.066 --> 00:11:00.366
Huh? Hey, wait!

198
00:11:00.433 --> 00:11:06.500
So, if Pikachu can Mega Evolve too, then I want to find out if Dedenne can.

199
00:11:06.566 --> 00:11:09.699
- Please tell me, please?
- Aw. What a shame.

200
00:11:09.766 --> 00:11:12.600
There’s no way Dedenne could have a Mega Evolution.

201
00:11:12.666 --> 00:11:15.199
What? Why not?

202
00:11:15.266 --> 00:11:18.933
- There.
- So, I think it's time we begin?

203
00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.933
- Hold on a second.
- Huh?

204
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.933
How do you know that there’s a Mega Stone in Geosenge Town anyway?

205
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.466
Our job is to know all of that stuff.

206
00:11:27.533 --> 00:11:32.233
Along with a Key Stone, it’s needed to facilitate a Pokémon’s Mega Evolution.

207
00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:37.666
Everybody knows that. A Pokémon will Mega Evolve with the use of two stones.

208
00:11:37.733 --> 00:11:40.300
You’re wrong. There are different Mega Stones.

209
00:11:40.366 --> 00:11:44.133
Each Pokémon requires its own specific Mega Stone to Mega Evolve.

210
00:11:44.199 --> 00:11:47.100
The Mega Stone in Geosenge Town is Lucarionite

211
00:11:47.166 --> 00:11:49.400
and only Lucario can Mega Evolve with it.

212
00:11:49.466 --> 00:11:51.233
-Huh?

213
00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.666
Professor Sycamore was talking about the same thing.

214
00:11:54.733 --> 00:11:58.100
He said Gardevoir’s Mega Stone was Gardevoirite.

215
00:11:58.166 --> 00:12:01.233
Uh, now that I think of it, he did say that.

216
00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:06.300
So what we’re saying is Pikachu won’t be able to Mega Evolve using Lucarionite.

217
00:12:06.366 --> 00:12:09.733
How could you forget something as important as that?

218
00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:14.466
All right, what kind of Mega Evolution Consulting Group are you?

219
00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:16.266
Who are you guys anyway?

220
00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:19.233
The jig’s up. It's show time!

221
00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.433
Pika?

222
00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.500
Huh?

223
00:12:22.566 --> 00:12:25.699
- Open this thing up!
- Pikachu.

224
00:12:25.766 --> 00:12:27.066
Huh?

225
00:12:27.133 --> 00:12:28.333
Team Rocket.

226
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.566
That’s our name. Don't wear it out.

227
00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:33.333
When uttered by twerps, it clouds its clout.

228
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.833
To protect the world from devastation.

229
00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.566
To unite all people within our nation.

230
00:12:38.633 --> 00:12:41.633
To denounce the evils of truth and love.

231
00:12:41.699 --> 00:12:45.166
To extend our reach to the stars above.

232
00:12:45.233 --> 00:12:46.900
- Jessie.
- And James.

233
00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:50.099
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light.

234
00:12:50.166 --> 00:12:53.300
Surrender now or prepare for a Mega-Evolved fight.

235
00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:56.733
- Meowth, that’s right!
- Wobbuffet!

236
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.599
Uh! Come back here, Team Rocket.

237
00:13:00.666 --> 00:13:02.466
-Pika! Pi!

238
00:13:02.533 --> 00:13:04.000
Pikachu!

239
00:13:04.066 --> 00:13:07.133
Who’s that Pokémon?

240
00:13:11.099 --> 00:13:13.199
It’s Lucario.

241
00:13:17.566 --> 00:13:18.900
Team Rocket?

242
00:13:18.966 --> 00:13:23.000
They’re really bad guys who are always trying to steal people’s Pokémon.

243
00:13:23.066 --> 00:13:27.433
Tiny twerp’s right. We populate a terrifying and mysterious organization

244
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:30.000
that performs unseemly acts of evil every day.

245
00:13:30.066 --> 00:13:32.400
All I care about is getting Lucario back.

246
00:13:32.466 --> 00:13:34.233
Blah, blah, blah.

247
00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.000
We’ll Mega Evolve both Lucario and Pikachu

248
00:13:37.066 --> 00:13:40.133
and create an invincible Mega-Evolved Pokémon posse

249
00:13:40.199 --> 00:13:42.500
the likes of which the world has never seen.

250
00:13:42.566 --> 00:13:44.400
Wobbuffet!

251
00:13:44.466 --> 00:13:48.066
Meanwhile, here’s a parting gift!

252
00:13:49.666 --> 00:13:53.099
- Smoked them again!
- Wobbuffet!

253
00:13:54.099 --> 00:13:55.433
Oh, man!

254
00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.400
Don’t worry. We’ll get Lucario and Pikachu back.

255
00:13:58.466 --> 00:14:02.199
But how do we find out where Team Rocket went?

256
00:14:02.266 --> 00:14:06.233
That’s easy. I have the perfect device for this situation.

257
00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:11.333
Ha! The future is now, thanks to science. Clemontic Gear on.

258
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.900
- I’ll handle this.
- Korrina.

259
00:14:14.966 --> 00:14:16.333
Korrina!

260
00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.266
- Huh?
- Ash.

261
00:14:18.333 --> 00:14:21.866
- Come on, Clemont, hurry up.
- Huh, coming.

262
00:14:21.933 --> 00:14:25.300
Our first stop is Geosenge Town to find the Lucarionite.

263
00:14:25.366 --> 00:14:28.766
Then we can locate the Pikachunite at a more leisurely pace.

264
00:14:28.833 --> 00:14:31.466
But how do we know that Pikachunite really exists?

265
00:14:31.533 --> 00:14:35.633
We don’t know for certain if Pikachu will even be able to Mega Evolve.

266
00:14:35.699 --> 00:14:39.500
Negative thinking prevents me from having a nice day, so stop it.

267
00:14:39.566 --> 00:14:41.366
Wobbuffet!

268
00:14:42.766 --> 00:14:45.900
Yipes. They’re trying to fly the coop.

269
00:14:47.033 --> 00:14:50.733
You’re wasting your move groove. That cage is attack-proof.

270
00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.866
Dig it. The only thing you lugs are going to get is tired.

271
00:15:09.566 --> 00:15:12.833
Pikachu! Lucario!

272
00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:22.000
-Maybe they didn’t come this way.

273
00:15:22.066 --> 00:15:24.599
Do you always have to run so fast?

274
00:15:24.666 --> 00:15:27.833
- Well, maybe you run too slow.
- Na-na!

275
00:15:35.266 --> 00:15:38.933
Yup. Lucario’s here. They’re not far away.

276
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:43.099
You can really sense where Lucario is? That’s incredible.

277
00:15:43.166 --> 00:15:45.633
Uh-huh. I can.

278
00:15:45.699 --> 00:15:49.433
The two of us have been together ever since we were young.

279
00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:54.866
We played together, laughed together, ate together,

280
00:15:54.933 --> 00:15:58.833
fought together, we grew up like siblings.

281
00:16:02.033 --> 00:16:04.833
Lucario and I share an unbreakable bond.

282
00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.333
That’s something that will never change.

283
00:16:13.466 --> 00:16:17.266
I just know. Lucario’s waiting for me to rescue it.

284
00:16:17.333 --> 00:16:20.033
Isn’t that little more than a hunch though?

285
00:16:20.099 --> 00:16:21.733
Yup, but I just know.

286
00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.300
Hey! Diantha said something like that as well.

287
00:16:25.366 --> 00:16:27.900
She and Gardevoir could sense each other.

288
00:16:27.966 --> 00:16:29.733
- I believe you.
- Huh?

289
00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:30.733
Huh?

290
00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.099
Pikachu and I have traveled all this way together, too.

291
00:16:34.166 --> 00:16:37.099
We’ve trusted and helped each other and battled as a team.

292
00:16:37.166 --> 00:16:40.733
It’s exactly the same for us as for you.

293
00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.233
Leave it to me.

294
00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:47.333
Uh! Pika!

295
00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:50.400
Maybe you should start collecting stamps or something.

296
00:16:50.466 --> 00:16:51.699
Wobbuffet!

297
00:16:54.966 --> 00:16:57.133
Pika! Pika!

298
00:17:00.699 --> 00:17:04.533
Pika! Pika! Pika! Pika! Pika! Pi!

299
00:17:04.599 --> 00:17:10.000
I guess you’ll just have to learn the hard way. Your Electro Ball is useless.

300
00:17:13.566 --> 00:17:17.000
Combining moves should be against the law!

301
00:17:22.166 --> 00:17:23.833
Huh! This way!

302
00:17:28.833 --> 00:17:30.833
Pika! Pika!

303
00:17:30.899 --> 00:17:32.733
-Pika!

304
00:17:35.899 --> 00:17:38.500
We wouldn’t dream of letting you leave so soon.

305
00:17:38.566 --> 00:17:41.500
Pika! Pika! Pika! Pika! Pi!

306
00:17:41.566 --> 00:17:43.500
Okay, Inkay, Psybeam.

307
00:17:43.566 --> 00:17:45.733
All right, Pumpkaboo, use Dark Pulse.

308
00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:48.600
Inkay!

309
00:17:54.833 --> 00:17:59.066
Playtime’s over. Now come with us like good little Twerp Pokémon.

310
00:17:59.133 --> 00:18:00.833
Wobbuffet!

311
00:18:00.899 --> 00:18:02.733
Pi...

312
00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.333
- Stop it, Team Rocket.
- Pika? Pika?

313
00:18:06.899 --> 00:18:08.600
- Oh!
- Incoming twerps.

314
00:18:08.666 --> 00:18:10.700
Lucario, are you all right?

315
00:18:10.766 --> 00:18:12.500
You okay, Pikachu?

316
00:18:12.566 --> 00:18:14.200
- Pika.
- All right!

317
00:18:14.266 --> 00:18:18.300
You got the Key Stone back from them. You’re the best, Lucario!

318
00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.800
Thank goodness we found you.

319
00:18:21.866 --> 00:18:23.466
Na-na-na!

320
00:18:23.533 --> 00:18:27.933
I say we settle this with a Pokémon Battle and may the worst twerp lose.

321
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.133
So how about a Tag Battle for your 100th in a row?

322
00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.733
Yeah. Let’s do this, Ash!

323
00:18:36.733 --> 00:18:38.899
- Ready, Pikachu?
- Pika!

324
00:18:38.966 --> 00:18:41.399
Let’s show them, Lucario.

325
00:18:41.466 --> 00:18:45.100
Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball.

326
00:18:45.166 --> 00:18:47.500
- Inkay, Psybeam.
- Inkay!

327
00:18:47.566 --> 00:18:49.866
Lucario, use Bone Rush.

328
00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:55.966
I didn't know you could do that with Bone Rush.

329
00:18:56.033 --> 00:19:01.033
We’re not through. Inkay, I want you to use Tackle on Lucario.

330
00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.266
Lucario, Power-Up Punch.

331
00:19:10.566 --> 00:19:12.233
Lucario did it again.

332
00:19:13.466 --> 00:19:17.100
- Inkay, no!
- Must I fix everything? Shadow Ball!

333
00:19:17.166 --> 00:19:19.566
All right, Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.

334
00:19:19.633 --> 00:19:24.833
Pikachu!

335
00:19:24.899 --> 00:19:29.000
We’re blasting off again.

336
00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:36.033
We did it. That’s 100 wins in a row.

337
00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:40.033
Uh-oh. I did it again. I forgot to get their footprints!

338
00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:44.200
Guess it’s too late now. No biggie, no biggie.

339
00:19:48.266 --> 00:19:52.266
We won 100 battles in a row and we’re definitely much stronger now.

340
00:19:52.333 --> 00:19:56.000
It’s time to head to Geosenge Town.

341
00:19:56.066 --> 00:19:59.066
Hey, can we go to Geosenge Town with you?

342
00:19:59.133 --> 00:20:02.133
I really want to see Lucario’s Mega Evolution.

343
00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.600
- Pikachu.
- I want to see that, too.

344
00:20:04.666 --> 00:20:08.166
- What a rare opportunity.
- Me, too! Me, too! Me, too!

345
00:20:08.233 --> 00:20:09.566
Na-na-na-na!

346
00:20:09.633 --> 00:20:13.666
We can’t pass up an opportunity to see the secrets behind Mega Evolution

347
00:20:13.733 --> 00:20:16.066
and the Mega Stone with our very own eyes.

348
00:20:16.133 --> 00:20:17.500
Uh...

349
00:20:17.566 --> 00:20:18.633
- Hm.
- Hm.

350
00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.433
I’ll show you Mega Lucario. You can come with us.

351
00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.633
Now that that’s settled, let’s go.

352
00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.933
Do we really have to run again?

353
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.666
Come on, Clemont.

354
00:20:29.733 --> 00:20:32.933
Hurry, hurry, big brother.

355
00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.933
Our heroes have unexpectedly run into Korrina,

356
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.933
the Shalour Gym Leader, and her partner, Lucario.

357
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.766
Now, as the search for Lucarionite begins,

358
00:20:41.833 --> 00:20:46.833
everyone heads for Geosenge Town, as the journey continues.
